# SABOTAGE: ADR-041 §11 / §6.1 — the CRM timeline custom.crm_refs OR-match is load-bearing.
#
# T97 destructively migrated CRM Activity into the canonical Work Task. A multi-anchored
# Activity (linked to BOTH a contact and a deal) becomes a Task whose PRIMARY subject anchor
# is one object (by precedence) while the FULL ref set survives in custom.crm_refs. The CRM
# detail timeline read (Samen.Web.CRM.Reads.activities_for_company/3) therefore OR-matches
# `subject_key/subject_id == crm.company` OR `custom.crm_refs.company_id == company_id`, so a
# Task primary-anchored to the contact still appears in the COMPANY timeline — the
# both-timelines preservation guarantee (§6.1). Without the crm_refs OR-branch that timeline
# entry silently disappears for every migrated multi-anchored Activity.
#
# This sabotage strips the crm_refs OR-branch from activities_for_company/3. The named test —
# which raw-inserts a crm.person-anchored Task whose company link lives ONLY in crm_refs and
# asserts it appears in BOTH timelines (with the company's own primary-anchored activity as
# the positive control) — MUST fail (the company-timeline assertion). Revert restores the
# branch byte-exact.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_detail_render_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MULTI-ANCHOR
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
@@ -208,9 +208,6 @@ def activities_for_company(mount, scope, company_id) do
     work_task_resource(mount)
     |> Ash.Query.ensure_selected(@timeline_fields)
-    |> Ash.Query.filter(
-      (subject_key == "crm.company" and subject_id == ^company_id) or
-        get_path(custom, ["crm_refs", "company_id"]) == ^company_id
-    )
+    |> Ash.Query.filter(subject_key == "crm.company" and subject_id == ^company_id)
     |> Ash.Query.sort(inserted_at: :desc)
     |> Ash.Query.limit(@detail_limit)
     |> Ash.read!(scope: scope)
